[x] google oauth login (web and app) @done
    -> ID-token flow (google_sign_in plugin -> POST /auth/google), not a redirect
       flow: no deep links / URL schemes needed. Skips email verification, since
       Google vouches for the address. Linking a password account to Google is
       irreversible (password is overwritten) and needs explicit confirmation:
       first call answers 409 google_link_required, client re-sends the same
       token with link_existing after the dialog. Also reachable from
       Settings -> "Sign in with Google instead".
    [ ] Google Cloud setup (mine): Web OAuth client (authorized JS origins:
        http://localhost:3000 + the Railway web URL) and an Android client
        (package com.poulsekora.poulse_kora_app + keystore SHA-1). Then set
        GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED / GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS on the backend and
        --dart-define=GOOGLE_SERVER_CLIENT_ID on the app.
    [ ] release keystore: android release builds still sign with the debug
        keystore, so google sign-in breaks the day a real one lands unless its
        SHA-1 is registered too
    [ ] password reset: there is still no forgot-password flow at all, so a user
        who loses their Google account has no recovery path


bugs:
[x] beta info banner onCLick popup not working 
[x] if existing users are not validated yet, displaying in the app looks not nice -> weird error messages instead of routing to validation page
    [x] additionally routing to validation page not always working properly
    [x] addtionally, code sending not working on first try every time
    -> app: _RouterRefreshNotifier only attached its profileProvider listener
       inside a *live* login transition callback; routerProvider is built after
       authReadyProvider resolves, so on a cold start with an already-stored
       token, authNotifierProvider was already resolved and that transition
       never fired - the listener never attached, so redirect never learned
       profile.isVerified and left unverified users stuck on /feed hitting the
       raw unverified_user error instead of /verify-email. Fixed by also
       attaching it eagerly at construction if already logged in.
       backend: on_after_register / resend both started the resend cooldown
       *before* awaiting send_email; an SMTP failure (no retry/timeout in
       app/core/email.py) then either 500'd /auth/register (account already
       created, so a retry just hit user_already_exists) or 500'd resend -
       either way leaving the cooldown active for up to 60s with no email ever
       sent. Fixed to only start the cooldown after a successful send, and to
       surface resend failures as a proper `email_send_failed` error instead
       of a crash.
[ ] a route can return null (e.g. get banner) -> check if best practise
[x] when an action failes (e.g. forwarding/dropping a post), the animation still plays -> perform the check before the animation

